[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue: the parser reads dates month first. Read
by tenant and channel instead of by subject line, its reports hold three problems. Each one now
has a ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser will not close #4471. The hint and the shift reports will keep coming.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## How the reports were placed

- **One id, one report.** The export pages overlap, so some reports appear twice. Each id counts once.
- **By tenant, not by intake tag.** A report's problem comes from its tenant's locale and booking
  form ([causes.ts](/kb/triage/dedupe)), not from `meta.intakeTag`. Intake guesses from the
  reporter's browser, and the guess is often wrong.
- **Shifts, counted twice.** The desk marked the reports where the date moved by one day instead of
  swapping (`desk-notes.json`). They are a different bug with their own ticket, and they stay
  counted under `parser`, where the desk files them by tenant.

## Why it was merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. All three
problems produce the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite"), so they landed in one ticket.
A new decision record should replace 0001; this page does not change it.

